[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3]

; The maze fixture: one empty dungeon room, built to the size the generator
; actually gives a maze. Owned by tools/directors/maze.gd.
;
; Underscore-prefixed like _atom_test.tscn and _lookdev.tscn -- it is a harness,
; not a room the game ships.
;
; **Why this is not _atom_test.tscn any more.** The maze's fixture beats used to
; stand a maze up in the proving ground, which is 22 m of slab with a 20 m
; interior and a showroom's worth of furniture in it -- a ledge, two pillars,
; two pushable blocks, two braziers -- so the director's first act was to free
; four node groups and say so. That worked while the maze was 12.4 x 9.3 m. It
; does not now: 5x5 cells at MazeRoom.CELL is 20.15 m across, which is WIDER
; than the chamber's interior, and the lantern apron would have put both
; lanterns a metre and a half behind the south wall. Every fixture beat would
; still have passed -- they press the lanterns by reference -- and that is
; precisely the failure MazeRoom.APRON's note is about, reproduced in the one
; place that is supposed to catch it.
;
; So: 27 m square, which is Dungeon.MAZE_ROOM, with nothing in it. A fixture the
; size of the thing it fixtures. The room the generator builds has doorways in
; it and this one does not, because a doorway is a hole the hero can walk out
; through mid-beat and beat F reports that as "stuck".

